"Forest Floor"
"Having passed through the dense foliage, you now stand in a lightly wooded
section of the forest, just north of a massive rock left by ancient glaciers. 
The face of the rock has been carved by the hand of nature, creating in it a
natural shelf upon which many devotions have been left over the centuries. 
All around, the glade teams with signs of life.  Insects buzz and crawl about
the area as they go about their lives.  The occasional seed falling from a
tree or bush and hitting the ground can be heard if one remains quiet and
still.  Rustling of nearby bushes caused by a slight, passing breeze creates
in this place a soothing atmosphere which lends itself readily to this already
tranquil refuge.  Near the base of a nearby tree, a large grouping of vines,
thickly covered in star-shaped leaves, sinuously winds its way up into the
lowest reaching branches of its host.  A fallen log, covered in vibrant green
moss, lays along the edge of the clearing, slowly rotting due to the elements
of nature and the constant passing of time.
"
